# Support modules

`tests/support/` holds every non-test file. Each module owns one area. Put new helpers in the owning
module; create a new module only for a new product area (one per area, named after it: `billing.ts`, `cases.ts`).

| Module         | Owns                                                                                                  |
| -------------- | ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |
| `env.ts`       | `.env` loading, `requireEnv`, `portalUrl`, `credentials`, `Portal` / `RoleKey` types                  |
| `errors.ts`    | `P1Error` and `failApp` / `failTestData` / `failAutomation`                                           |
| `session.ts`   | `SAVED_SESSIONS`, `authFile`, `signIn`, `openSession`, `gotoPortal`, `waitForShell`                   |
| `report.ts`    | `describeCheck`, `recordActual` (test annotations)                                                    |
| `test-data.ts` | `TEST_DATA`: every fixed record name / id the checks rely on                                          |
| `ui.ts`        | Generic page reading: `readPage`, `readDialog`, `selectedOption`, `checkedLabel`, `flat`, `stamp`, `escapeRegExp`, `RECORD_FILE` |
| `tasks.ts`     | Task list and task dialog flows, due-date picker                                                      |
| `states.ts`    | Admin user / location state fields and the Book appointment eligibility panel                         |
| `timezones.ts` | Profile timezone, timezone selects, calendar visit times                                              |

## Dependency direction

`errors`, `env`, `test-data`, `ui` ← `session` ← area modules (`tasks`, `states`, `timezones`, …) ← specs.
(`env` may import `errors`; `ui` imports nothing local.)
Area modules never import each other or any spec. No barrel `index.ts`; import from the module directly.

## Helper rules

- Export only what a spec calls. Keep step helpers (`openUser`, `commit`, …) module-private.
- Every exported function gets a one-line `/** */` saying what it does and what it returns.
- Helpers fail with `failApp` / `failTestData` / `failAutomation` and a message a reader can act on.
- Record names come from `TEST_DATA`; accounts from `credentials()`. No literals for either.
- Escape any `TEST_DATA` value used inside a `RegExp` with `escapeRegExp`.
- Before adding a helper, search `tests/support/` for an existing one. Extend it rather than adding a near copy.
- Delete helpers that no spec uses any more.

## Saved sessions

Adding a role to `SAVED_SESSIONS` makes `tests/auth.setup.ts` sign it in on every run. Add it only when a spec
needs that role's saved session, and add its `<ROLE>_EMAIL` / `<ROLE>_PASSWORD` to the "Signed in once per run"
block of `.env.example`.
